WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.480
- Alright y'all, we're
back celebrating women

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:05.520
smashing glass ceilings
in sports, on the field,

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:07.450
the courts, and the sidelines.

00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:10.630
My next guest is a remarkable
13 year old athlete

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:12.510
who plays softball,

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:14.080
basketball,

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.570
volleyball,

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:18.659
and soccer, cause, well why
the hell not? (Kelly laughs)

00:00:18.659 --> 00:00:20.323
(audience laughing)

00:00:20.323 --> 00:00:24.010
All while maintaining a
4.0 grade point average.

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:26.100
So she's every parent's dream.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:29.410
But her ultimate dream is to
be a sports ball color analyst,

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:31.013
so check her out in action.

00:00:31.957 --> 00:00:35.033
- Hi, I'm McKenzie Kesh
and welcome to Dodgerton.

00:00:35.033 --> 00:00:39.370
The Dodgers are the top
team in MLB without a doubt.

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:41.200
So you can't argue with that.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:45.060
When the Dodger's whoop-it,
they do not do their job.

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:47.340
The Women's National
Team deserves more money

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:48.300
than the men's.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.670
The men's, how many world
cups have they been to?

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:51.980
Less than the women's.

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:53.620
What, did they qualify?

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:54.820
No, they didn't.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:58.100
And the NCAA Men's March
Madness Tournament underdogs

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.500
have been winning and
busting people's brackets,

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:01.666
including mine.

00:01:01.666 --> 00:01:04.400
(inaudible)

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:05.350
Don't get me started.

00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:06.840
- What's so good about Lakers?

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:09.240
- What's so good about Celtics, hmm?

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:11.417
I'm McKenzie Kesh signing off.

00:01:11.417 --> 00:01:12.860
(audience claps)

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:14.590
- Oh my god. You are great.

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:16.323
Everybody say hello to McKenzie!

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:19.640
(audience cheers)

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:22.160
You are so great.

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:24.729
And hilarious, by the way,
your timing is so many,

00:01:24.729 --> 00:01:26.030
so much passion.

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:27.230
And your videos, I love it.

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:29.050
Have you always loved sports?

00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:31.560
- Yes. I can't live without sports.

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:33.550
I love sports for as
long as I could remember.

00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:35.930
I started playing baseball
when I was five years old

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:38.040
and I was the only girl on my team.

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:40.300
And I was just as good as all the boys.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:43.010
- I love your confidence. Oh my gosh.

00:01:43.010 --> 00:01:45.910
So why do you dream of
being a color analyst

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:49.280
and just for inquiring minds want to know,

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:50.693
what is a color analyst?

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:53.960
- Well, there are two
types of broadcasters.

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:55.820
There's a play-by-play analyst

00:01:55.820 --> 00:01:58.000
who basically tells you
exactly what's happening

00:01:58.000 --> 00:01:58.940
in the game.

00:01:58.940 --> 00:02:01.120
And then there's a color
analyst, what I want to be,

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:04.330
and they share your facts
and opinions about the game

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:06.440
and give you more insight of their stories

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:08.110
because they normally have
played the game before.

00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:10.530
- Yeah. And give them little more sass.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:11.363
- Yes.

00:02:11.363 --> 00:02:13.180
Cause that's what I love
about you, McKenzie.

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:15.840
Well, we have two sports
ball analysts who know all

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:17.460
about your skills and passion.

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:18.400
They want to meet you.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:19.320
Do you want to meet them?

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:20.153
- Yes, please.

00:02:20.153 --> 00:02:24.350
Okay. Well, one is a
two-time WNBA all-star.

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:26.200
She still plays for the Sparks

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:29.010
and she's an NBA analyst for ESPN.

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:31.800
The other is an Olympic gold medalist

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:34.790
and a major league
baseball analyst for ESPN.

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:37.013
They're each a whole lotta woman, y'all.

00:02:41.847 --> 00:02:44.440
All right everybody, say
hi to Chiney Ogwumike

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:46.339
and Jessica Mendoza!

00:02:46.339 --> 00:02:49.460
(audience claps)

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:51.530
Wait, where is she? (Kelly exclaims)

00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:53.571
- Oh my goodness. Oh my god.

00:02:53.571 --> 00:02:55.229
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:55.229 --> 00:02:57.209
- [Chiney] I got you some gifts.

00:02:57.209 --> 00:02:58.525
- [Kelly] Yes!

00:02:58.525 --> 00:02:59.423
- [Chiney] Hey girl.

00:02:59.423 --> 00:03:00.256
- Hi.

00:03:00.256 --> 00:03:01.872
- [Chiney] You are so amazing.

00:03:01.872 --> 00:03:02.705
- [McKenzie] Thank you so much.

00:03:02.705 --> 00:03:04.138
- [Chiney] And so I got you some presents

00:03:04.138 --> 00:03:05.340
from the LA Sparks.

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:06.173
- Thank you.

00:03:06.173 --> 00:03:10.660
- [Kelly] Yes. So, I have to ask you.

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:11.493
Chiney, I'll start with you.

00:03:11.493 --> 00:03:13.230
What do you think of McKenzie's talent?

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:14.200
She's hilarious.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:16.700
- I wish I was you when I was younger.

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:19.590
I mean, your personality
jumps off the screen.

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:20.600
You are confident.

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:22.290
You're intelligent.

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:23.152
You've got it made.

00:03:23.152 --> 00:03:24.270
- [McKenzie] Thank you so much.

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:25.103
- Amazing.

00:03:25.103 --> 00:03:26.780
- It means so much coming from you.

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:29.730
- [Kelly] Oh my God.
What about you Jessica?

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:30.660
- Oh my gosh.

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:34.040
Hi, McKenzie. I love all
the photos by the way.

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:35.270
How are you?

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:36.250
- I'm doing amazing.

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:37.470
- [Jessica] Oh my gosh.

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:39.130
Chiney shows up with like a gift bag,

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:42.070
I'm like, "Dang it. I want
to do that." (Jessica laughs)

00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:42.903
Oh my gosh.

00:03:42.903 --> 00:03:44.200
I had to point out one thing though.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:45.960
You are honest.

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:47.260
Oh my gosh. I love it.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:49.100
You are so real.

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:49.933
Do you know what?

00:03:49.933 --> 00:03:53.240
It takes women like decades
to be able to find their voice

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:55.270
and to be able to say it loud and proud.

00:03:55.270 --> 00:03:56.937
And you just call on out
that men's world cup,

00:03:56.937 --> 00:03:59.440
"How many world cup does the men have?"

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:01.310
Oh I love that.

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:04.577
- It is my favorite
part of the whole video.

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:06.427
"How many? Oh, oh that's sad."

00:04:06.427 --> 00:04:07.722
"How many of the women won?"

00:04:07.722 --> 00:04:09.780
(Kelly laughs)

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:10.840
So here's my thing.

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:13.650
So you each have something
to tell McKenzie, right?

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:14.570
So you want to go for it, Jessica?

00:04:14.570 --> 00:04:16.020
You want to talk first?

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:16.853
- Oh yeah.

00:04:16.853 --> 00:04:18.870
So first of all, Mackenzie,
we need to hook up.

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:21.300
We need to beat up. I heard
you talking about the Dodgers.

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:22.400
I know that's your team

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:25.710
and I want to be able to hang
with you at Dodgers stadium.

00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:27.860
So I know that you're
in Southern California.

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:30.770
So you and I have got to meet up.

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:32.120
If you have any questions

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:34.730
the fact that your softball or baseball.

00:04:34.730 --> 00:04:37.070
I play baseball first
too girl, and I love it.

00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:37.960
I feel like our paths

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:40.130
are definitely gonna keep connecting.

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:41.030
- [McKenzie] Thank you.

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:42.643
Oh my gosh, thank you so much.

00:04:42.643 --> 00:04:44.642
- [Kelly] She's fighting the tears.

00:04:44.642 --> 00:04:45.706
So what about you, Chiney?

00:04:45.706 --> 00:04:48.290
- Can I hang out with y'all
at Dodger stadium too?

00:04:48.290 --> 00:04:49.850
Jess, isn't it open
invitation? (Jessica laughs)

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:51.220
Okay, good.

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:52.370
I can't let my team

00:04:52.370 --> 00:04:53.203
- You should get my some Sparks shoes.

00:04:53.203 --> 00:04:54.640
- [Chiney] Okay yeah. There we go.

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:56.590
I can't let my team go to the dust.

00:04:56.590 --> 00:04:58.350
So I would love, once we have fans,

00:04:58.350 --> 00:05:01.330
for you to come court side
and watch the LA Sparks play.

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:02.550
That'd be so much fun.

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:03.740
You could rock your jersey.

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:06.180
You've got your own custom Jersey in here.

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:08.410
And working for ESPN, I'd love

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:10.920
if you'd be able to
shadow me on my radio show

00:05:10.920 --> 00:05:13.330
and just hang out with the guys
and give them the business.

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:14.980
You could be like our guest correspondent.

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:17.700
- That would be amazing.
Thank you so much.

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:19.024
Thank you Ms. Jessica.

00:05:19.024 --> 00:05:22.226
- Oh my God. I love you. She
said, "Thank you Ms. Jessica"

00:05:22.226 --> 00:05:25.587
(Kelly laughs) Oh my god.

00:05:25.587 --> 00:05:29.240
A big thanks to Play-by-play
sports broadcasting cams

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:31.380
for telling us all about McKenzie.

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:32.770
She's amazing.

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:35.030
And we're so glad we got to hang with you.

00:05:35.030 --> 00:05:37.630
Can't wait to have you back
after those experiences.

